eased full-year outlook reflects strong first-half orders and financial performance, as well as confidence in the execution of our strategic priorities and our ability to sustain this momentum through the second half of fiscal 2027,\" said John Linker, Executive Vice President and Chief Financial Officer. Based on year-to-date performance and its outlook, the Company is increasing its guidance for fiscal 2027, ending March 31, 2027 as follows:\nMetric Updated FY27 Outlook Prior FY27 Outlook\nNet sales $2.13 billion to $2.17 billion $2.09 billion to $2.15 billion\nAdjusted EBITDA5 $425 million to $440 million $405 million to $420 million\nAdjusted EPS5 $2.00 to $2.15 $1.90 to $2.10\nFiscal 2027 guidance reflects updated assumptions, based on final purchase price accounting linked to the Kito Crosby Acquisition, of:\nMetric Updated FY27 Outlook Prior FY27 Outlook\nInterest expense $185 million to $190 million $185 million to $190 million\nAmortization expense $130 million to $135 million $135 million to $140 million\n"}
